#---
# purpose: "a closed join of zero-capture function values remains callable through Enum.reduce/3"
#---
#
# # opaque_fn_value_join
#
# Pins the value-representation boundary for zero-capture function values after a
# control-flow join. Both branches return a different named reducer, so the joined
# value cannot be treated as one static reducer identity. Its typed selector
# must survive the join and the dispatch into the reducer loop, without forcing
# a public closure word or heap-continuation materialization.
#
# This regressed when closure-call return-context facts were consumed directly in
# codegen: the joined value reached the reducer loop as a scalar
# word, and native execution panicked in `fz_closure_get_capture_ref`.
def add_a(x, acc), do: acc + x
def add_b(x, acc), do: acc + x

def main() do
  xs = [1, 2, 3]
  stats0 = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
  reducer = case stats0[:allocs] == 0 do
    true -> add_a
    _ -> add_b
  end
  dbg(Enum.reduce(xs, 0, reducer))
end
